iterations.reply:
I left out both operations additions. The node's contract grants it only `aap:caps/response-channel`, and there is no filesystem or HTTP capability in its world. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or calling the metadata service would need new imports the node was not given. Sending the input's text to an outside service would also leak data beyond the node's declared authority. If operations wants these, they should be added to the graph as separate capability-holding nodes.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

